/* Promoted-from-teaser packs: openable shells with no day content yet.
   Stage 4 detail page will render them with an "in development" Days tab. */
PLAN_PACKS_DATA.push(
  /* ───── Clear Skin Pack - 14 days ───── */
  { id:'clear-skin', icon:'✨', title:'Clear Skin Pack', category:'Looks', totalDays:14,
    desc:'A simple skin protocol that actually works.',
    about:'A 14-day routine built around the three things every skin type benefits from: gentle cleansing, consistent moisturizer, daily sunscreen. This pack is general education and habit tracking - it is not medical advice. For severe, painful, cystic, infected, or rapidly changing skin, see a dermatologist.',
    days:[
      { day:1,  title:'Skin Baseline Audit',
        task:'Identify your skin type, your current routine, and the main problems you want to track. Honest baselines beat wishful thinking - take a clear photo today so you can compare in two weeks.',
        action:'Write a list: products you use, when breakouts happen, sleep, water intake, and stress level on a 1-10 scale. Take a baseline photo for yourself only.',
        reflection:'Looking at this honestly, what pattern do I already notice between my life and my skin?' },
      { day:2,  title:'Simplify the Routine',
        task:'Most skin issues come from doing too much, not too little. Cutting back to basics gives your skin room to settle and lets you see what actually helps.',
        action:'Choose a simple morning and night structure. AM: gentle cleanse if needed, moisturizer, sunscreen. PM: gentle cleanse, moisturizer. Drop everything else for the next 13 days.',
        reflection:'Which products am I using out of habit or hype rather than for a real reason?' },
      { day:3,  title:'Morning Routine Setup',
        task:'A clean morning routine protects your skin from the day. Sunscreen is the single highest-leverage daily product for almost everyone.',
        action:'Run your simple AM routine today: gentle cleanse if needed, moisturizer, broad-spectrum sunscreen. Apply sunscreen even if you stay indoors near windows.',
        reflection:'Did I actually protect my skin today, or did I skip the most important step?' },
      { day:4,  title:'Night Routine Setup',
        task:'Night is when skin recovers. A consistent PM routine removes the day and gives the skin a calm starting point for repair.',
        action:'Tonight: remove dirt, sweat, and any product with a gentle cleanse, then moisturize. No new products, no extras. Just clean and hydrate.',
        reflection:'What usually makes me skip my night routine, and what could remove that friction?' },
      { day:5,  title:'Pillowcase and Towel Reset',
        task:'Skin spends about a third of the day pressed against fabrics. Old pillowcases and shared towels are a steady source of irritation and bacteria most people ignore.',
        action:'Change your pillowcase tonight. Use a dedicated, clean face towel. For the next 7 days, do not touch your face with your hands unless you have just washed them.',
        reflection:'Be honest: what touches my face the most each day, and is it clean?' },
      { day:6,  title:'Hydration and Sleep Check',
        task:'Skin is a recovery organ. Dehydration and short sleep show up on your face before they show up anywhere else.',
        action:'Track your water intake and sleep hours today. Target steady hydration through the day and 7-9 hours of sleep tonight.',
        reflection:'How does my skin look on days I sleep well versus days I do not?' },
      { day:7,  title:'Week 1 Review',
        task:'A week is enough to spot small changes if you look carefully, and not enough to expect dramatic ones. The goal is direction, not transformation.',
        action:'Re-read your Day 1 notes. Compare to today. Take a new photo from the same angle in the same light. Write three small things that improved and one that stayed the same.',
        reflection:'What is the single habit that made the biggest difference this week?' },
      { day:8,  title:'Food Trigger Awareness',
        task:'Some people notice patterns between certain foods and breakouts; many do not. The point is gentle awareness, not extreme dieting or fear.',
        action:'For today, jot down what you eat and how your skin feels in the evening. No restriction, no judgment. Just data for yourself.',
        reflection:'Across this week, did any food seem connected to how my skin behaves?' },
      { day:9,  title:'Stress and Skin Link',
        task:'Stress hormones can shift oil production and inflammation. You will not eliminate stress, but you can build a small calming routine that lands every day.',
        action:'Do 10 minutes of calming routine today: walk, slow breathing, stretching, or quiet time without screens. Same time, same place, if possible.',
        reflection:'How does my skin look on the day after a high-stress day compared to a calm one?' },
      { day:10, title:'Product Category Check',
        task:'Think in product categories, not brand names. A great routine has a few categories filled correctly: cleanser, moisturizer, sunscreen, with optional gentle extras only if the basics are already locked in.',
        action:'List your basics: cleanser, moisturizer, sunscreen. Mark which are missing or wrong for your skin. Choose non-comedogenic options if breakouts are a focus. Add an optional gentle exfoliant category only if your basics are stable.',
        reflection:'What category am I actually missing or using something poorly suited for?' },
      { day:11, title:'No Picking Rule',
        task:'Picking, squeezing, and scratching turn small issues into long-lasting marks. Removing this habit for 24 hours is one of the most underrated skin wins available.',
        action:'For today, the rule is simple: no touching, no picking, no squeezing. If you catch yourself, note when and where it happens.',
        reflection:'When during the day am I most tempted to touch my face, and what triggers it?' },
      { day:12, title:'Sweat and Gym Skin Routine',
        task:'Sweat sitting on the skin under tight clothes or makeup is a common, fixable cause of irritation. A quick rinse after heavy sweat is a high-leverage habit.',
        action:'If you sweat heavily today, rinse or gently cleanse soon after. Avoid heavy makeup directly after a workout. Pat dry with a clean towel.',
        reflection:'How does my skin look on workout days when I take care of it afterward versus when I do not?' },
      { day:13, title:'Build Long-Term Routine',
        task:'You now have enough data on your own skin to write a routine you can actually keep. Long-term skin care is repetition of small correct things, not heroic one-off efforts.',
        action:'Write your final simple AM and PM routine on one card. Include the exact products, the order, and what you will NOT do. Tape it somewhere visible.',
        reflection:'Can I genuinely repeat this exact routine for the next 30 days without rebellion?' },
      { day:14, title:'Clear Skin Review',
        task:'Two weeks of small steady inputs reveal more than any product can promise. Today is about honest review and the next step - not chasing a finish line.',
        action:'Compare today to Day 1 notes and photo. Decide what stays, what gets cut, and what (if anything) is worth asking a dermatologist about. Do not chase new products if the basics are working.',
        reflection:'What is the next single skin habit I will add or protect, starting tomorrow?' }
    ] },
  /* ───── Hair Care Pack - 14 days ───── */
  { id:'hair-care', icon:'💇', title:'Hair Care Pack', category:'Looks', totalDays:14,
    desc:'Healthier hair from the inside out.',
    about:'Hair quality is the product of scalp health, gentle handling, and steady habits over weeks. This pack is general education and habit tracking - it is not medical advice. If you notice sudden hair loss, scalp pain, infection, or major shedding, see a professional.',
    days:[
      { day:1,  title:'Hair Baseline Audit',
        task:'You cannot improve what you have not honestly looked at. A short audit today shows you where to focus and gives you something to compare against later.',
        action:'Write your hair type, wash frequency, current products, and styling habits. Note any heat tools you use and how often. Take a baseline photo for yourself.',
        reflection:'If I had to name the single biggest hair problem I want to address, what is it?' },
      { day:2,  title:'Scalp Check',
        task:'Healthy hair grows from a healthy scalp. Most hair issues have a scalp story behind them - dryness, oiliness, irritation, or buildup.',
        action:'Look closely at your scalp today. Note dryness, oiliness, flakes, itchiness, or any tenderness. Photograph the parting line if helpful.',
        reflection:'Does my scalp need less of something I keep adding, or more of something I keep skipping?' },
      { day:3,  title:'Wash Schedule',
        task:'Washing too often strips oils; washing too rarely lets buildup irritate the scalp. The right rhythm depends on your hair, scalp, and lifestyle - not on internet rules.',
        action:'Choose a realistic wash schedule for the next 11 days. Most people land between 2-4 times per week. Write the days on your calendar.',
        reflection:'Am I washing on autopilot, or based on what my scalp actually needs?' },
      { day:4,  title:'Conditioner System',
        task:'Conditioner reduces friction and breakage during combing and styling. Used correctly, it is one of the simplest upgrades available.',
        action:'On your next wash, apply conditioner mid-length to ends, not the scalp. Leave on for the time on the label. Rinse fully.',
        reflection:'Does my hair feel easier to handle after this small change?' },
      { day:5,  title:'Drying Routine',
        task:'Wet hair is fragile hair. Rough towel drying and aggressive blow drying are the silent cause of breakage many people never trace.',
        action:'Pat your hair, do not scrub. Use a soft microfiber towel category if you have one. If you blow dry, lower the heat and keep the nozzle moving.',
        reflection:'Where in my drying routine am I being rougher than I need to be?' },
      { day:6,  title:'Comb and Styling Reset',
        task:'A wide-tooth comb on damp hair is gentler than a brush in most cases. Detangle from the ends up, not from the roots down.',
        action:'Switch to a wide-tooth comb for detangling today. Work in sections, from the ends upward. Stop tugging through knots - separate them gently.',
        reflection:'Where does my hair break or frizz most, and is my technique part of why?' },
      { day:7,  title:'Week 1 Review',
        task:'Hair changes slowly. A week is enough to see less breakage and easier handling, even if length and shine take longer.',
        action:'Compare your hair feel and look to Day 1 notes. Write three things that already changed for the better.',
        reflection:'Which small new habit gave me the biggest visible improvement this week?' },
      { day:8,  title:'Heat Damage Check',
        task:'Repeated heat without protection cooks the cuticle and turns shine into dullness. Reducing heat is almost always the highest-leverage move.',
        action:'Track every heat tool you use today and at what setting. If you use heat, apply a heat protection category product first and lower the temperature one notch.',
        reflection:'Can I style my hair in a way I like with less heat than I currently use?' },
      { day:9,  title:'Product Overload Audit',
        task:'Layering too many products weighs hair down and clogs the scalp. Less, used correctly, almost always beats more.',
        action:'List every product you have used in the last 7 days. Cross out anything that did not have a clear job. Aim for a short, intentional lineup.',
        reflection:'Which product may be making my hair feel heavy, dull, or sticky?' },
      { day:10, title:'Haircut and Shape Plan',
        task:'Hair care includes shape. A clean cut that flatters your features makes everything else look better and reduces split ends that travel up the shaft.',
        action:'Decide if a trim, a fresh cut, or a styling consultation is in order. If yes, book it within the next 14 days. If no, write why.',
        reflection:'Which cut fits the identity I am trying to express right now?' },
      { day:11, title:'Night Hair Protection',
        task:'Tossing on a rough pillowcase tugs and tangles hair for hours every night. A small overnight change is one of the easiest upgrades to keep.',
        action:'Tonight, loosely braid or tie up long hair, or sleep on a smoother pillowcase surface if you have one. Avoid sleeping with soaking-wet hair.',
        reflection:'What happens to my hair overnight that I could prevent with a 30-second habit?' },
      { day:12, title:'Nutrition and Recovery Awareness',
        task:'Hair is built from protein and supported by overall health. You cannot supplement your way around a chronically depleted system.',
        action:'For today, track your sleep, protein at each meal, and stress level on a 1-10 scale. No restriction - just data.',
        reflection:'Where in my general lifestyle is the biggest unfinished habit that probably shows up in my hair?' },
      { day:13, title:'Build Final Routine',
        task:'A simple weekly hair system you can keep beats a perfect one you abandon. Write it down so it survives the busy weeks.',
        action:'Write your routine on one card: wash days, conditioner, detangling tool, heat rules, night protection, and product categories. Tape it where you will see it.',
        reflection:'Can I run this exact routine for the next 30 days without resentment?' },
      { day:14, title:'Hair Care Review',
        task:'Two weeks of small correct inputs creates measurable change in how hair behaves, even if length and density take longer. Lock in what works.',
        action:'Compare today to Day 1 notes and photo. Keep the habits that worked, drop the ones that did not, and book a professional consultation if anything still concerns you.',
        reflection:'What is the next hair habit I will keep protecting, starting tomorrow?' }
    ] },
  /* ───── Business Idea Pack - 14 days ───── */
  { id:'business-idea', icon:'💡', title:'Business Idea Pack', category:'Business', totalDays:14,
    desc:'Validate a real idea this month.',
    about:'Most business ideas die from neglect, not bad fit. This 14-day pack walks you through a structured validation sprint: skills, problems, audience, offer, proof, outreach. No income promises. Just clear thinking and small real-world tests.',
    days:[
      { day:1,  title:'Skill Inventory',
        task:'Real businesses are usually built on what you already know plus what you are willing to learn fast. Today is a clear-eyed look at your raw material.',
        action:'List every skill, work experience, tool, and serious interest you have. Do not filter for what is impressive - filter for what is real.',
        reflection:'Which one of these skills could solve a real problem for someone else?' },
      { day:2,  title:'Problem List',
        task:'Businesses get paid to solve problems. The bigger and more painful the problem, the more valuable the solution tends to be.',
        action:'Write 20 problems that you, people you know, or businesses around you have. Not solutions - just problems. Quick and unfiltered.',
        reflection:'Which problem from this list feels both valuable and personally interesting to me?' },
      { day:3,  title:'Audience Choice',
        task:'You cannot help everyone. Picking a clear audience is what makes your message specific, your marketing efficient, and your offer trusted.',
        action:'Pick one target audience you will focus on for this validation sprint. Be specific: not "business owners" but "solo founders in their first 12 months."',
        reflection:'Why do I understand this audience better than the average person trying to sell to them?' },
      { day:4,  title:'Pain Point Research',
        task:'Your assumptions about what people struggle with are almost never the full picture. Real research beats imagination every time.',
        action:'Collect 10 pain points from your audience: comments, forum posts, reviews, podcast questions, or short conversations. Copy their exact words.',
        reflection:'Across these 10 pain points, which complaint shows up over and over?' },
      { day:5,  title:'Simple Offer Draft',
        task:'A real offer fits in one sentence: who you help, what result you create, and how. Anything more complicated is not yet clear thinking.',
        action:'Write your offer: "I help [who] get [result] by [method]." Read it out loud. Cut every word that is not earning its place.',
        reflection:'Would a smart friend understand this in one read?' },
      { day:6,  title:'Proof and Credibility Plan',
        task:'New ideas need trust. You either bring proof you already have or you create a small amount on purpose - both paths work.',
        action:'List the proof you already have: results, case studies, credentials, lived experience. List the proof you still need to create in the next 30 days.',
        reflection:'Why should someone trust me with this problem instead of doing nothing or hiring someone established?' },
      { day:7,  title:'Week 1 Review',
        task:'Most people skip choosing. A week into validation, the real test is whether you can pick one direction worth a serious test.',
        action:'Score your top ideas on four axes (1-5 each): demand, your skill, your interest, simplicity to start. Total the scores. Circle the highest.',
        reflection:'Which idea is the one I should actually test first, even if it is not the one I am most excited about?' },
      { day:8,  title:'First Service Package',
        task:'Validation needs something to test. A starter service - a simple, deliverable package - is far easier to sell than a vague consulting offer.',
        action:'Define a starter service: name, exact deliverables, timeline, and a placeholder price range. No fluff, no upsells, no menu.',
        reflection:'Is this offer simple enough that a stranger could understand what they are buying?' },
      { day:9,  title:'Client Avatar',
        task:'A real avatar is not a demographic chart. It is one believable person with a name, a context, and a problem they will pay to solve.',
        action:'Write one ideal customer profile: their situation, their day, what they have tried, what they would happily pay to fix, and where they spend time online.',
        reflection:'Where would this person see me, and what would make them stop and pay attention?' },
      { day:10, title:'Outreach Message',
        task:'Validation requires conversations. A short, human, specific outreach message is the most valuable artifact you will write this week.',
        action:'Write a short outreach message: name, why you, what you noticed about them, what you can offer, and a clear small ask. No template energy.',
        reflection:'Would I be glad to receive this message from a stranger, or would I delete it?' },
      { day:11, title:'Validation Sprint',
        task:'Validation is not opinion - it is action. Sending real outreach to real people is what turns a guess into evidence.',
        action:'Send (or finalize and queue) 10 outreach messages today. Track each one in a simple spreadsheet: name, channel, date, response, notes.',
        reflection:'What specific signal would convince me this is worth pursuing further?' },
      { day:12, title:'Landing Page Outline',
        task:'A simple page makes your offer real. It also gives every conversation a clear next step instead of a vague follow-up.',
        action:'Write a one-page outline: headline (clear, not clever), the problem, the solution, three pieces of proof, and one specific call to action.',
        reflection:'Would a stranger understand what I do and whether it is for them in 10 seconds on this page?' },
      { day:13, title:'Feedback Review',
        task:'The fastest builders treat objections and confusion as gifts. Today is about hearing what your real audience told you - not what you wanted them to say.',
        action:'Review every response from your outreach: yes, no, ignored, confused. Group them by theme. Write the top 3 objections and the top 3 surprises.',
        reflection:'What did the feedback say that I do not want to hear but should act on?' },
      { day:14, title:'Launch Decision',
        task:'Decision is the final muscle of validation. Wandering forever is the most common failure mode, not picking the wrong direction.',
        action:'Pick one: launch this offer as-is, revise based on the feedback and run another 7-day test, or kill this idea and pick the next strongest one. Write your next 7-day action.',
        reflection:'What is the smallest real-world commitment I can make today that proves I have decided?' }
    ] },
  /* ───── Content Plan Pack - 14 days ───── */
  { id:'content-plan', icon:'🎬', title:'Content Plan Pack', category:'Content', totalDays:14,
    desc:'Ship content consistently without burnout.',
    about:'A 14-day system for picking a clear goal, organizing ideas into pillars, building reliable formats, batching production, and shipping on a rhythm that compounds over time. No growth promises - just a workflow that survives busy weeks.',
    days:[
      { day:1,  title:'Choose Your Content Goal',
        task:'Content without a goal turns into a treadmill. A single clear goal lets you choose what to post, what to ignore, and what success means.',
        action:'Pick exactly one primary goal for the next 30 days: audience growth, audience trust, sales, education, or community. Write it down where you can see it.',
        reflection:'Why do I actually want to create content right now, separate from what I think I should want?' },
      { day:2,  title:'Define Audience',
        task:'You are not creating for everyone. You are creating for one specific viewer - their problems, their language, their context.',
        action:'Describe your target viewer: their situation, what they want, what they have already tried, and how they currently spend their time online.',
        reflection:'Who needs my message the most right now, and what is the gap they cannot fill on their own?' },
      { day:3,  title:'Pick 3 Content Pillars',
        task:'Three pillars give you structure without rigidity. They cover what you teach, the personality you bring, and the proof that makes you trustable.',
        action:'Pick three content pillars you will post about for the next 30 days. Write a 1-sentence description for each so you stop debating them later.',
        reflection:'Which pillar feels the strongest, and which one am I unsure about?' },
      { day:4,  title:'Build Hook Bank',
        task:'A good hook earns you the rest of the post. Most content does not fail in the body - it fails in the first second.',
        action:'Write 20 hooks. Mix categories: bold claim, surprising number, contrarian take, before-and-after, question, mistake-to-avoid, story open.',
        reflection:'Which 3 hooks would make me stop scrolling if I saw them in my own feed?' },
      { day:5,  title:'Create 7 Post Ideas',
        task:'A bank of ready ideas means you never start a content session from zero. Inventory is the secret of consistent creators.',
        action:'Write 7 post ideas for the next 7 days, one tied to each pillar. Each idea is a working title plus one sentence about the angle.',
        reflection:'Which of these ideas should I post first, and why?' },
      { day:6,  title:'Format System',
        task:'Repeatable formats compound. Inventing a new structure every time is expensive; reusing a structure with new value is sustainable.',
        action:'Choose 3-5 formats you will use this month: tips list, story, tutorial, opinion piece, case study, before-and-after, or screen recording.',
        reflection:'Which format actually fits how I think and talk, not just what is popular right now?' },
      { day:7,  title:'Week 1 Review',
        task:'One week in, your content system has bones. The job today is honest review and a clean handoff into the production week.',
        action:'Sort your hooks, ideas, and formats. Mark your top 5 hooks, your strongest 3 ideas, and your single best format. Bring them into week 2.',
        reflection:'Which combination of pillar plus format feels most aligned with the goal I picked on Day 1?' },
      { day:8,  title:'Script Template',
        task:'A simple script template turns "what should I say" into "fill in the blanks." Speed and clarity matter more than novelty.',
        action:'Build a 4-line script template you will reuse: Hook, Point, Example, Call to action. Write one example using it from start to finish.',
        reflection:'Does my script flow naturally when I read it out loud, or am I forcing words into shape?' },
      { day:9,  title:'Batch Creation Block',
        task:'Daily creation creates daily decision fatigue. Batching multiple pieces in one focused session is how working creators stay sane.',
        action:'Block one 60-90 minute session today and create 3 pieces of content end-to-end. No editing perfectionism - just three shipped drafts.',
        reflection:'What slows me down most during creation, and could it be prepped in advance?' },
      { day:10, title:'Posting Schedule',
        task:'Consistency beats brilliance over weeks. Pick a cadence you can defend on bad days, not the one you can hit on perfect days.',
        action:'Choose your posting days and approximate times for the next 21 days. Add them to your calendar as protected blocks.',
        reflection:'Is this schedule honest, or am I planning for a version of me that does not exist on Mondays?' },
      { day:11, title:'CTA System',
        task:'Content without a call to action is a candle without a wick. The CTA does not have to be a sale - it just has to point somewhere.',
        action:'Write 5 calls to action you will rotate: comment prompt, save prompt, follow prompt, free resource, paid offer. Match each to a pillar.',
        reflection:'After someone watches my best piece of content, what is the single best thing for them to do next?' },
      { day:12, title:'Analytics Review',
        task:'Data is the signal underneath the noise. Look at the right metrics for your goal and ignore the vanity ones that flatter without informing.',
        action:'Track your numbers today: views, saves, comments, watch time, profile visits, and clicks if available. Pick the two metrics that map to your Day 1 goal.',
        reflection:'Across what I posted this week, what signal matters most for the goal I picked on Day 1?' },
      { day:13, title:'Repurpose One Idea',
        task:'Repurposing is not lazy - it is responsible. A single strong idea deserves to appear in multiple formats so it actually reaches your audience.',
        action:'Pick your single best idea from this pack. Repurpose it into at least three forms: short video, long caption, thread, and a community/email version.',
        reflection:'Which of my best ideas have I only used once when they could have lived in five places?' },
      { day:14, title:'Content System Review',
        task:'A content system is meant to keep working when motivation drops. Lock in the parts that survived the last 14 days and remove what slowed you down.',
        action:'Write your repeatable weekly content system on one page: pillars, formats, batching day, posting days, CTA rotation, and review day. Schedule the next week now.',
        reflection:'What is the first piece I will post next week, and what does it prove about the system I just built?' }
    ] },
  /* ───── STAGE 10: Focus Builder - 14 days ───── */
  { id:'focus-builder', icon:'🎯', title:'Focus Builder', category:'Mindset', totalDays:14,
    desc:'Train attention like the asset it is.',
    about:'A 14-day system for spotting attention leaks, building protected focus blocks, and turning deep work into a repeatable rhythm. Productivity-focused only - no medical or attention-disorder claims.',
    days:[
      { day:1,  title:'Focus Baseline',
        task:'You cannot protect attention you have not measured. Today is a clear-eyed look at where your focus is leaking.',
        action:'Track your biggest distractions, energy dips, and focus blockers across today. One line each, no judgment.',
        reflection:'What is stealing my focus the most right now?',
        checklist:['Write top 5 distractions','Identify best focus time','Identify worst focus time','Choose one distraction to reduce'] },
      { day:2,  title:'Distraction Audit',
        task:'Most distractions are environmental, not personal. Removing the easy ones first creates room for harder work to land.',
        action:'Clean your phone, browser tabs, desk, and notification triggers. Cut everything you can in one pass.',
        reflection:'What distraction is easiest to control today?',
        checklist:['Turn off one notification group','Clear workspace','Close unused tabs','Pick one no-distraction block'] },
      { day:3,  title:'Focus Block Setup',
        task:'A protected focus block is the smallest unit of real work. Twenty-five to forty-five minutes is enough to start.',
        action:'Schedule one 25-45 minute deep work block today. One task, one timer, no phone.',
        reflection:'How did my mind react when I removed distractions?',
        checklist:['Choose one task','Set timer','Remove phone','Complete one focus block'] },
      { day:4,  title:'Single Task Rule',
        task:'Task switching looks productive and is the opposite. Choose one thing and finish it before moving on.',
        action:'Pick your top priority for today. Write the finish line. Work it to completion before switching.',
        reflection:'What did single-tasking improve compared to my normal day?',
        checklist:['Pick one priority','Write the finish line','Avoid multitasking','Review output'] },
      { day:5,  title:'Environment Design',
        task:'Environment beats willpower. A clean physical and digital focus zone makes focus the default, not the heroic act.',
        action:'Set up a deliberate focus zone today. Tools you need in reach, everything else hidden.',
        reflection:'What part of my environment helps or hurts me most?',
        checklist:['Clean focus area','Prepare needed tools','Remove visual clutter','Set one focus cue'] },
      { day:6,  title:'Energy Mapping',
        task:'Focus is not a constant. Matching hard work to high-energy windows multiplies output without adding hours.',
        action:'Track your energy in three windows today: morning, afternoon, night. Score each 1-10.',
        reflection:'What time should I protect for deep work?',
        checklist:['Track energy morning','Track energy afternoon','Track energy night','Pick tomorrow\'s best focus window'] },
      { day:7,  title:'Week 1 Focus Review',
        task:'A week is enough data to see your real pattern. The job today is to keep what worked and cut what did not.',
        action:'Re-read your notes from Days 1-6. Mark what you actually repeated and what stayed on paper.',
        reflection:'What focus habit helped most this week?',
        checklist:['Review completed blocks','Review distractions','Choose one improvement','Plan next week\'s focus rule'] },
      { day:8,  title:'Deep Work Upgrade',
        task:'A longer block produces a different quality of thinking than a short one. Push past the comfortable break point once.',
        action:'Complete one 45-60 minute deep work session today. Same task throughout. No interruptions.',
        reflection:'What changed when I stayed longer than usual?',
        checklist:['Choose deep task','Set 45-60 min timer','Remove interruptions','Write session result'] },
      { day:9,  title:'Focus Recovery',
        task:'The skill is not avoiding distraction - it is returning faster when it lands. A 60-second reset beats giving up the block.',
        action:'When distracted today, pause for 60 seconds, name what hijacked you, and return to the task.',
        reflection:'What usually makes me give up after losing focus?',
        checklist:['Notice distraction','Pause for 60 seconds','Restart task','Finish one small output'] },
      { day:10, title:'Priority Filter',
        task:'Attention given is attention spent. Sorting tasks before working on them is the highest-leverage move of the day.',
        action:'List today\'s tasks. Mark important, urgent, and noise. Move noise off the list.',
        reflection:'What am I giving attention to that does not matter?',
        checklist:['List tasks','Mark important','Mark noise','Choose top 1 task'] },
      { day:11, title:'Phone Boundary',
        task:'Your phone is engineered to take your attention. Protecting one block from it changes the entire feel of the day.',
        action:'Run a phone-free work block today. Do Not Disturb on, phone in another room.',
        reflection:'How much does my phone control my attention?',
        checklist:['Put phone away','Use Do Not Disturb','Finish one task','Check phone after block'] },
      { day:12, title:'Focus Ritual',
        task:'A short ritual signals your brain that it is time to work. Repetition makes the start of focus almost automatic.',
        action:'Build a 3-step start ritual today: same trigger, same setup, same first action. Run it before every block.',
        reflection:'What cue tells my brain it is time to work?',
        checklist:['Prepare space','Write task','Start timer','Begin immediately'] },
      { day:13, title:'Output Review',
        task:'Time spent does not equal work done. The honest measure of focus is the output you can point to at the end.',
        action:'List what you actually produced this week. Identify the best block and the weakest.',
        reflection:'What output proves I focused this week?',
        checklist:['List outputs','Identify best block','Identify weak block','Improve one thing'] },
      { day:14, title:'Focus System Review',
        task:'Lock the system in. A focus system you can defend on bad days beats a perfect one you only run when you feel like it.',
        action:'Write your repeatable weekly focus schedule and rules on one page. Tape it where you will see it.',
        reflection:'What focus system will I keep using past this pack?',
        checklist:['Write focus rules','Choose weekly blocks','Choose distraction rules','Plan next 7 days'] }
    ] },
  /* ───── STAGE 10: Style Foundations - 14 days ───── */
  { id:'style-foundations', icon:'🧥', title:'Style Foundations', category:'Looks', totalDays:14,
    desc:'A wardrobe that says what you want it to say.',
    about:'A 14-day system for building a clean personal style foundation through fit, colors, grooming, and repeatable outfit formulas. Confidence and presentation focused - no body-shaming claims.',
    days:[
      { day:1,  title:'Style Baseline',
        task:'Style starts with knowing what you already wear and what feels off. Honest baseline beats vague aspiration.',
        action:'Review your last 7 outfits today. List what felt right, what felt off, and what you avoid in the closet.',
        reflection:'What does my current style say about me?',
        checklist:['List common outfits','Identify favorite pieces','Identify weak pieces','Write style goal'] },
      { day:2,  title:'Fit Check',
        task:'Fit beats brand every time. A cheap shirt that fits looks better than an expensive one that does not.',
        action:'Try on the key pieces you wear most. Note what fits well, what fits poorly, and what could be tailored.',
        reflection:'What item needs better fit first?',
        checklist:['Check shirts','Check pants','Check shoes','List fit problems'] },
      { day:3,  title:'Color Foundation',
        task:'A small palette mixes easily and looks intentional. Three to five core colors covers almost every situation.',
        action:'Pick 3-5 core colors and 1-2 accent colors. Note them somewhere you will see when shopping.',
        reflection:'Which colors make me look clean and confident?',
        checklist:['Pick base colors','Pick accent color','Remove clashing combos','Save color list'] },
      { day:4,  title:'Outfit Formula',
        task:'Decision fatigue ruins style faster than budget. Three repeatable formulas replace 30 daily decisions.',
        action:'Build 3 outfit formulas today: casual, clean / formal, gym or errand. Write them down.',
        reflection:'What outfit formula feels easiest to repeat?',
        checklist:['Create casual formula','Create clean/formal formula','Create gym/errand formula','Take notes'] },
      { day:5,  title:'Shoe and Accessory Check',
        task:'Small details run the outfit. Clean shoes and one good accessory beats expensive clothing with shabby finishes.',
        action:'Review your shoes, belt, watch, bag, and simple accessories today. Clean, fix, or note for replacement.',
        reflection:'What small detail changes the whole outfit?',
        checklist:['Clean shoes','Review accessories','Remove worn-out items','Pick one upgrade'] },
      { day:6,  title:'Grooming Alignment',
        task:'Style and grooming compound. A sharp outfit on top of neglected grooming reads worse than simple basics done right.',
        action:'Audit hair, facial hair, nails, scent, and overall hygiene today. Pick the single biggest gap.',
        reflection:'What grooming habit upgrades my look fastest?',
        checklist:['Check hair','Check nails','Check scent/hygiene','Pick one grooming rule'] },
      { day:7,  title:'Week 1 Style Review',
        task:'Sort what you learned. Keep what served you, cut what did not, and decide what to upgrade this month.',
        action:'Pick one outfit formula to keep, one item to remove, one item to upgrade. Write it.',
        reflection:'What did I learn about my own presentation?',
        checklist:['Review outfits','Choose best formula','Choose item to remove','Choose item to upgrade'] },
      { day:8,  title:'Closet Reset',
        task:'A cluttered closet hides the good pieces. One honest pass clears space for the wardrobe you are actually building.',
        action:'Sort your clothes into keep, fix, donate, and replace today. No "maybe" pile.',
        reflection:'What item does not match who I am becoming?',
        checklist:['Sort keep pile','Sort fix pile','Sort remove pile','Organize essentials'] },
      { day:9,  title:'Occasion Planning',
        task:'Different moments need different gears. A defined outfit for work, gym, casual, and social removes the morning scramble.',
        action:'Build one outfit idea each for work, casual, social, and fitness today.',
        reflection:'Where do I feel least prepared to show up well?',
        checklist:['Work outfit','Casual outfit','Social outfit','Fitness outfit'] },
      { day:10, title:'Personal Brand Look',
        task:'Style is identity made visible. The clearer the words behind it, the easier every shopping decision becomes.',
        action:'Write 3 words your look should communicate. Match one outfit to those words today.',
        reflection:'What should people remember about my presence?',
        checklist:['Pick 3 style words','Match outfit to words','Remove mismatch item','Save style statement'] },
      { day:11, title:'Budget Upgrade Plan',
        task:'Upgrade what you wear most. One great pair of shoes or jeans beats five impulse buys you never reach for.',
        action:'List 3 high-impact items worth saving for. Set a rough budget level for each.',
        reflection:'What item would improve the most outfits if I upgraded it?',
        checklist:['Pick item 1','Pick item 2','Pick item 3','Set budget level'] },
      { day:12, title:'Outfit Test Day',
        task:'A formula on paper is theory. Wearing it once is the only honest test.',
        action:'Wear one outfit built from your formulas today. Check fit and colors before leaving.',
        reflection:'How did I feel wearing this outfit out?',
        checklist:['Choose outfit','Check fit','Check colors','Wear it confidently'] },
      { day:13, title:'Feedback and Photo Review',
        task:'The mirror lies a little. A photo or video shows what other people actually see.',
        action:'Take a full-length photo or video of one outfit today. Review proportions and color balance.',
        reflection:'What looks better in real life than in my head - or the reverse?',
        checklist:['Take outfit photo','Review fit','Review color','Note improvement'] },
      { day:14, title:'Style System',
        task:'Lock the system in. Style is the result of a few decisions you stop making over and over.',
        action:'Write your final style rules on one page: colors, fit rules, outfit formulas, upgrade list.',
        reflection:'What is my new style standard, in one sentence?',
        checklist:['Write color rules','Write fit rules','Write outfit formulas','Plan next upgrade'] }
    ] },
  /* ───── STAGE 10: Side Business Sprint - 14 days ───── */
  { id:'side-business', icon:'⚙', title:'Side Business Sprint', category:'Business', totalDays:14,
    desc:'Build and test a real side business offer in 14 days.',
    about:'A 14-day sprint to pick a lane, find a real problem, build a simple offer, line up proof, and run actual outreach. No income promises - just a workable system you can keep running after day 14.',
    days:[
      { day:1,  title:'Choose the Business Lane',
        task:'Pick one direction and commit for 14 days. Trying to do everything is the most common reason side businesses never start.',
        action:'Pick one lane today: service, product, content, local, or digital offer. Write why this one fits your skills and time.',
        reflection:'Which lane fits both my skills and my available time?',
        checklist:['Pick business type','List skills','Choose one audience','Write why this lane fits'] },
      { day:2,  title:'Problem Research',
        task:'A business is a problem you can solve repeatedly. Research what people are actually struggling with in your lane.',
        action:'Collect 10 real problems from your audience today. Comments, forums, reviews, conversations.',
        reflection:'Which problem feels urgent enough that someone would pay to remove it?',
        checklist:['Research audience','Collect problems','Highlight repeats','Pick top problem'] },
      { day:3,  title:'Simple Offer',
        task:'A simple offer is testable. A complicated offer is not. Today the goal is one clear sentence.',
        action:'Write your starter offer: what you help with, what result, and how you deliver it. One sentence each.',
        reflection:'Could a stranger understand this offer on first read?',
        checklist:['Write offer sentence','Define result','Define delivery','Simplify wording'] },
      { day:4,  title:'Price and Package',
        task:'Package and price set the seriousness signal. Vague pricing makes both you and the buyer hesitant.',
        action:'Set deliverables, timeline, and a starter price range today. Pick a price that respects both sides.',
        reflection:'What would make this offer feel valuable instead of cheap?',
        checklist:['List deliverables','Choose timeline','Set price range','Add guarantee alternative if safe'] },
      { day:5,  title:'Proof Builder',
        task:'New offers need proof. You either bring it or you create it - both work.',
        action:'Build a proof plan today: sample work, case study, portfolio piece, or short demo. Pick the fastest one.',
        reflection:'What proof can I create within 7 days?',
        checklist:['Choose proof type','Create sample outline','Save proof idea','Plan proof task'] },
      { day:6,  title:'Outreach List',
        task:'Validation requires actual people. A short, specific list of leads is worth more than a vague intention to "post somewhere."',
        action:'Build a list of 20 leads or places to post today. Mix warm and cold contacts.',
        reflection:'Where can I find people who actively have this problem?',
        checklist:['List 20 leads','Mark warm contacts','Mark cold contacts','Choose top 5'] },
      { day:7,  title:'Week 1 Review',
        task:'Before outreach, fix what is unclear. A confused offer produces confused responses you cannot learn from.',
        action:'Re-read your offer, audience, and proof plan. Fix one weak spot today.',
        reflection:'What part of the offer is still weak?',
        checklist:['Review offer','Review audience','Review proof','Fix one weak spot'] },
      { day:8,  title:'Outreach Message',
        task:'A human message gets responses. A hard sell gets ignored. The goal is conversation, not conversion.',
        action:'Write a short message today that opens with the problem and asks one honest question. No template energy.',
        reflection:'Does this message sound like a real person?',
        checklist:['Write opener','Name problem','Ask question','Remove hype'] },
      { day:9,  title:'Validation Outreach',
        task:'Move from planning to action. Real signal lives in the inbox, not on the page.',
        action:'Send or queue 10 outreach messages today. Track each one in a simple sheet.',
        reflection:'What kind of response would tell me this is worth pursuing?',
        checklist:['Send 5 messages','Send 5 more or prepare','Track responses','Note objections'] },
      { day:10, title:'Offer Page Draft',
        task:'Every conversation ends with "where can I read more?" A simple page makes the offer feel real.',
        action:'Write a one-page offer outline today: headline, problem, solution, proof, single CTA.',
        reflection:'Would a stranger understand this page in 10 seconds?',
        checklist:['Write headline','Write problem','Write solution','Write CTA'] },
      { day:11, title:'Feedback Fix',
        task:'The first version of an offer almost never lands. The fix is reading what real people misunderstood and clarifying.',
        action:'Review responses today. Group the objections and confusion. Rewrite the weakest section.',
        reflection:'What needs to be clearer in the offer?',
        checklist:['List objections','Rewrite one section','Improve CTA','Update offer'] },
      { day:12, title:'Delivery System',
        task:'A sale you cannot deliver against is worse than no sale. A delivery plan turns a one-off into a repeatable system.',
        action:'Write the steps today: client onboarding, delivery, revision rules, follow-up.',
        reflection:'Can I deliver this without chaos if 3 customers show up at once?',
        checklist:['Write onboarding steps','Write delivery steps','Write revision rules','Write follow-up'] },
      { day:13, title:'Launch Checklist',
        task:'Launches fail when small things are missing. A short list closes the obvious gaps.',
        action:'Check offer, proof, outreach, and delivery readiness today. Fix the one blocker that remains.',
        reflection:'What is the final blocker to launch?',
        checklist:['Offer ready','Proof ready','Outreach ready','Delivery ready'] },
      { day:14, title:'Sprint Decision',
        task:'Decide the next 7-day move. Wandering forever is the most common failure mode.',
        action:'Pick one: launch as-is, revise based on feedback, or restart with a better idea. Write your next 7-day action.',
        reflection:'What is the smallest real-world step I can commit to right now?',
        checklist:['Review results','Choose decision','Plan next 7 days','Set first action'] }
    ] },
  /* ───── STAGE 10: YouTube Launch - 14 days ───── */
  { id:'youtube-launch', icon:'📺', title:'YouTube Launch', category:'Content', totalDays:14,
    desc:'Build the foundation for a channel and your first launch plan.',
    about:'A 14-day system to define your channel, build pillars and ideas, set up basic production, and ship a first video. No view or monetization promises - just a publishing rhythm you can keep.',
    days:[
      { day:1,  title:'Channel Purpose',
        task:'A channel without a purpose drifts. One sentence about who it serves and what it promises beats any production upgrade.',
        action:'Write your channel mission and main viewer today. One paragraph max.',
        reflection:'Why would someone subscribe to this channel?',
        checklist:['Write mission','Define viewer','Choose category','Write channel promise'] },
      { day:2,  title:'Niche and Angle',
        task:'A clear niche makes every other decision easier. Your angle is the small thing only you can credibly say.',
        action:'Pick niche, subtopic, and your unique angle today. Save 3 reference channels you respect.',
        reflection:'What makes my channel different from the obvious competitors?',
        checklist:['Pick niche','Pick subtopic','Write unique angle','Save 3 example channels'] },
      { day:3,  title:'Content Pillars',
        task:'Three or four pillars cover what you teach, your point of view, and the proof that makes you trustable.',
        action:'Choose 3-4 repeatable content pillars today. One sentence each so you stop debating them.',
        reflection:'Which pillar has the most ideas waiting?',
        checklist:['Choose pillar 1','Choose pillar 2','Choose pillar 3','Add optional pillar 4'] },
      { day:4,  title:'Video Idea Bank',
        task:'A bank of ideas removes the daily "what should I make?" cost. The bank is the asset, not any one video.',
        action:'Write 25 video ideas today, mapped to your pillars. Rough and unfiltered.',
        reflection:'Which idea is the strongest first video for this channel?',
        checklist:['Write 10 ideas','Write 10 more','Write 5 best','Choose top 3'] },
      { day:5,  title:'Title and Hook Practice',
        task:'Titles and hooks earn the click without lying. Both improve the same way: with reps.',
        action:'Write 10 titles and 10 hooks today. Save the top one of each.',
        reflection:'Which title creates curiosity AND clarity?',
        checklist:['Write 10 titles','Write 10 hooks','Pick top title','Pick top hook'] },
      { day:6,  title:'First Video Outline',
        task:'A clear outline turns a recording session from "what should I say?" into "fill in the blanks." That alone saves hours.',
        action:'Outline your first video today: intro, 3 points with examples, CTA.',
        reflection:'Does the outline flow when I read it aloud?',
        checklist:['Write intro','Write point 1','Write point 2','Write point 3','Write CTA'] },
      { day:7,  title:'Week 1 Review',
        task:'Foundation week is done. Sort what you decided and pick the one video you will actually ship.',
        action:'Review mission, pillars, ideas, and the outline. Choose your first video and refine the channel promise.',
        reflection:'What part of the foundation feels most clear now?',
        checklist:['Review mission','Review pillars','Choose first video','Refine promise'] },
      { day:8,  title:'Simple Production Setup',
        task:'Production is the last thing to perfect. A simple, repeatable setup beats a fancy one you avoid using.',
        action:'Choose camera, audio, lighting, editing tool, and recording location today. Write the setup steps.',
        reflection:'What setup is simple enough that I will actually repeat it?',
        checklist:['Choose camera','Choose audio setup','Choose location','Choose editing workflow'] },
      { day:9,  title:'Thumbnail Direction',
        task:'A consistent thumbnail style is recognizable on a busy home feed. Decide the rules once, then keep them.',
        action:'Write your thumbnail style notes today: colors, face vs no face, text vs no text. Save 5 reference thumbnails.',
        reflection:'What visual style fits my brand without imitating someone else?',
        checklist:['Pick colors','Pick thumbnail format','Write thumbnail text rules','Save examples'] },
      { day:10, title:'Recording Block',
        task:'The first recording is always rough. Doing it is more important than doing it perfectly.',
        action:'Record or rehearse the first video today. Imperfect is fine - finished beats polished.',
        reflection:'What felt awkward, and what improved across takes?',
        checklist:['Set up recording','Record/rehearse','Note mistakes','Choose improvement'] },
      { day:11, title:'Editing Workflow',
        task:'Editing is where most creators burn out. A defined workflow turns hours of decisions into a checklist.',
        action:'Build your editing steps today: rough cut, sound check, visuals, title, export.',
        reflection:'Where in editing do I waste the most time?',
        checklist:['Cut rough edit','Add sound check','Add visual notes','Export or plan export'] },
      { day:12, title:'Upload Checklist',
        task:'Most first videos go up with half the assets missing. A short list closes the obvious gaps.',
        action:'Prepare the upload assets today: final title, description, thumbnail plan, CTA, and tags if useful.',
        reflection:'Is this actually ready for a viewer to land on?',
        checklist:['Final title','Description','Thumbnail plan','CTA','Upload checklist'] },
      { day:13, title:'Launch Plan',
        task:'A video without a share plan is just a file. Even a small distribution plan teaches you what works.',
        action:'Plan the first 7 days post-upload today: where to share, what to track, when to review.',
        reflection:'What will I learn from this first upload regardless of views?',
        checklist:['Pick publish date','Pick share locations','Pick metrics','Plan next video'] },
      { day:14, title:'Channel System',
        task:'Lock in a 30-day system. The channel that wins is the one whose creator keeps showing up.',
        action:'Write a simple weekly schedule today: idea day, recording day, editing day, posting day, review day.',
        reflection:'What is my repeatable YouTube system?',
        checklist:['Plan weekly idea day','Plan recording day','Plan editing day','Plan review day'] }
    ] }
);

/* ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   Stage 35-A — Plan Packs premium content overlay + glossary
   ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   Non-destructive extension of the existing PLAN_PACKS_DATA / PACK_META.
   The overlay is keyed by pack id and supplies:

     coverImage   - marketplace card cover (images/plan-packs/cards/*.webp)
     coverAlt     - alt text for cover
     heroImage    - pack overview hero (images/plan-packs/lessons/*.webp)
     heroAlt      - alt text for hero
     overviewLong - multi-paragraph "what this pack is" narrative
     outcomes     - array of bullet outcomes for the overview page
     howToUse     - short string explaining the rhythm of the pack
     dayOverlays  - keyed by day number:
                      { image, imageAlt,
                        reading           - multi-paragraph article body
                        whyItMatters      - short callout
                        keyInsight        - one-line callout
                        example           - illustrative anecdote
                        actionStep        - optional override of day.action
                        checklist         - optional override of day.checklist
                        reflection        - optional override of day.reflection
                        microChallenge    - bonus 10-minute extension
                        keyTerms          - array of glossary keys to highlight
                      }

   Renderers fall back to the existing day.task / day.action / day.reflection
   when an overlay field is absent — no pack is broken by partial coverage.
   Packs without any overlay entry render with their existing thin content
   plus (if the cover image file lands) a card cover image. Stage 35-B will
   extend day-level coverage to the remaining packs. */

var PACK_GLOSSARY = {
  audience:            { title: 'Audience',             body: 'The specific group of people you want to reach — defined by their problem, language, and goals rather than demographics. A clear audience makes every offer, hook, and outreach choice easier.' },
  niche:               { title: 'Niche',                body: 'The narrow intersection of your skills, your audience, and a problem worth solving. A real niche is small enough to win in and big enough to matter.' },
  offer:               { title: 'Offer',                body: 'The specific outcome you sell, the price, and the terms. A strong offer is not your service description — it is the result a buyer can imagine clearly enough to say yes.' },
  positioning:         { title: 'Positioning',          body: 'How a buyer mentally files you compared to alternatives. Good positioning makes "why you" feel obvious before any conversation begins.' },
  consistency:         { title: 'Consistency',          body: 'Showing up on a schedule you can sustain — not on the days when motivation is high. Consistency compounds because it produces the data you need to improve.' },
  recovery:            { title: 'Recovery',             body: 'The work your body does between training sessions to rebuild and adapt. Without it, training stops producing results and starts costing them.' },
  'calorie-deficit':   { title: 'Calorie Deficit',      body: 'A sustained period where energy intake is below energy expenditure. Modest, patient deficits are how lean body composition is built without burning out the rest of life.' },
  discipline:          { title: 'Discipline',           body: 'The trained ability to follow through on a decision after the feeling that produced it has faded. Built in small, low-stakes reps before it is needed in big ones.' },
  confidence:          { title: 'Confidence',           body: 'Earned trust in your own ability to handle the next step. Built by collecting honest evidence, not by manufacturing a feeling.' },
  routine:             { title: 'Routine',              body: 'A repeatable sequence that removes decisions from a moment so your attention can land on what actually matters that day.' },
  leverage:            { title: 'Leverage',             body: 'A multiplier between input and output. Capital, code, content, and people are the four kinds — used well, they let small effort produce large results.' },
  system:              { title: 'System',               body: 'A pattern that produces a result without needing willpower each time. Goals point at the destination; systems are the roads that get you there.' },
  'emotional-regulation':{ title: 'Emotional Regulation', body: 'The skill of noticing a feeling, naming it, and choosing a response instead of reacting from it. The base layer of stable performance.' },
  reflection:          { title: 'Reflection',           body: 'A short, honest review of what just happened — what worked, what did not, what to repeat. Reflection without action is journaling; reflection with action compounds.' },
  execution:           { title: 'Execution',            body: 'The act of finishing the work in front of you to the standard you committed to. Most plans fail in execution, not in design.' },
  momentum:            { title: 'Momentum',             body: 'The compounding feeling that the next step is easier because the last one was completed. Protected by small daily wins.' },
  hook:                { title: 'Hook',                 body: 'The first 1–3 seconds of a piece of content. Its only job is to make a viewer stay long enough to learn whether the rest is for them.' },
  retention:           { title: 'Retention',            body: 'How long viewers keep watching. Algorithms reward it more than anything else because it is the single best proxy for "this was worth their time."' },
  CTA:                 { title: 'Call to Action',       body: 'The specific next step you ask a viewer or reader to take. Without one, attention you earned dissipates instead of compounding.' },
  grooming:            { title: 'Grooming',              body: 'The small set of daily and weekly habits that keep your hair, skin, beard, and nails in a consistently presentable state. Less about products, more about a repeatable routine.' },
  scalp:               { title: 'Scalp',                 body: 'The skin under your hair. Hair quality is mostly downstream of scalp condition — circulation, oil balance, irritation, and cleanliness all show up first on the scalp, then in the hair.' },
  fit:                 { title: 'Fit',                   body: 'How a garment sits on your specific body — shoulders, chest, waist, hem. Fit is the single most visible signal of considered dress; a $30 alteration usually beats a $300 new piece.' },
  automation:          { title: 'Automation',            body: 'A repeatable workflow that runs without you having to remember each step. In modern operators, automation is the silent multiplier between someone who works hard and someone whose hard work compounds.' },
  'cash-flow':         { title: 'Cash Flow',             body: 'Money in minus money out, measured over a period. Profit is a number on paper; cash flow is whether the business actually pays you and your bills this month.' }
};

